  !>                 The leading (k + 1) by n part of each A_i must contain the upper
  !>                 triangular band part of the Hermitian matrix, with the leading
  !>                 diagonal in row (k + 1), the first super-diagonal on the RHS
  !>                 of row k, and so forth.
